# Kept out of the distributed archive.
#
# Entries are exact relative file paths -- modkit matches them literally, so a
# bare "tests/" silently does nothing. Add the file, not the directory.

# The suite requires engine test infrastructure (tests.modkit) and engine
# modules (src.world.Collision, src.world.gen2.World), which is a private
# require against the shipped package, and `pack` treats warnings as fatal.
# It only means anything inside an engine checkout.
tests/rby_run_forrest_test.lua

# The two end-to-end drivers reach tests/drivers/util.lua, which lives in the
# engine and not here, and are run through POKEPORT_DRIVER against a checkout.
# Same reason as the suite above: outside one they are unrunnable files taking
# up room in a player's install.
tests/drivers/route4_climb_test.lua
tests/drivers/gold_climb_test.lua

# docs/images/ is deliberately NOT ignored. README.md ships inside the archive
# and points at those six frames with relative paths, so dropping them would
# put broken images in the one document a player actually opens. Thirty
# kilobytes is the right price for that.
